  "id": "COMPOUND:23954 - PROTEIN:6153",
  "verbalization": "Fumiquinazoline B appears to interact with Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like through a series of intermediate targets, including Thioredoxin, Teyin, and Rhetsinine. These targets are all involved in metabolic pathways that are modulated by the enzyme Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The evidence suggests that Fumiquinazoline B may act as a modulator of these pathways, potentially influencing the activity of Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like. The presence of multiple distinct targets implies that Fumiquinazoline B may exert its effects through different mechanisms, possibly by interfering with the redox state of thioredoxin or by activating or inhibiting other enzymes in the pathway. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Fumiquinazoline B and Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, suggesting a possible role in metabolic regulation or disease pathogenesis.",
